.TH TWODRIVE 1 "October 2026" "TwoDrive" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
twodrive \- OneDrive files on demand for GNOME
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B twodrive
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
TwoDrive maintains a local cache and exposes OneDrive through FUSE.
Writes are durable locally before upload; local success does not confirm
remote completion. Run status to inspect pending operations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login, logout
Sign in using a browser or remove the local account authorization.
.TP
.B status, sync, mount
Inspect status, refresh remote metadata, or run the filesystem mount.
.TP
.BI "pin " path
Keep a file or directory available locally.
.TP
.BI "unpin " path
Cancel explicit and inherited keep-local preferences without deleting cache.
For directories, block ancestor policy while preserving independently pinned descendants.
.TP
.BI "release " path
Release synchronized cached data without removing remote files.
.TP
.B cache prune
Prune eligible synchronized cache entries.
.TP
.B retry-deletes
Schedule retained failed cloud deletions for another attempt.
.TP
.B settings
Open the GNOME settings application.
.TP
.B help
Display the complete command summary.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/twodrive/
contains private configuration. Data and cache paths follow XDG conventions.
Do not share token files, cache databases or upload session URLs.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR twodrive-daemon (1),
.BR twodrive-settings (1),
.BR twodrive-tray (1)
.PP
https://github.com/LumiaBlack51/twodrive
